    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on exploiting stolen base opportunities against high-delivery-time pitchers. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.12) is our premier start of the day, as he benefits from a massive 93% efficiency rating against the slow-moving delivery of Fedde, alongside a favorable 5.37 xERA matchup. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (75.84) grades out as a \"Strong\" play; while he holds a solid base projection, his score is bolstered by a favorable platoon edge against Ober and a 87% SB conversion projection against the pitcher's glacial cadence. We are also riding the momentum of **Carson Benge** (67.23), who draws a juicy matchup against Rodr\u00edguez, whose 6.75 xERA is the most exploitable spot on the board for our outfield unit.\n\nThe toughest tactical decision today involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished with a respectable 46.83, narrowly missing the cut behind the superior platoon and order-based projections of our utility and middle infield slots. While **Chase Meidroth** is trending upward, his neutral matchup against Rea lacked the dynamic upside offered by **Junior Caminero** (61.60) or **Hyeseong Kim** (61.33). Meanwhile, we are managing significant downside risk at the top of the order: both **Trea Turner** (49.79) and **Kyle Schwarber** (48.24) are facing the elite arm of Skenes, whose 2.96 xERA heavily suppressed their projections. While their raw talent and batting order spots keep them in the lineup, they are essentially \"floor\" plays today; we will be monitoring these at-bats closely, as the proximity to a sub-40 efficiency rating is uncomfortably high. Owners should also note that **Zac Veen** remains stationed in Albuquerque, as we await his potential recall to provide a further boost to our SB-starved bench.",
